#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Editing Tools"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comment/Uncomment"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Comment and Uncomment commands, available from the <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu> menu allow you to add or remove comment markers to the selection, "
"or the current line if no text is selected, if comments are supported by the "
"format of the text you are editing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The rules for how commenting is done are defined in the syntax definitions, "
"so if syntax highlighting is not used, commenting/uncommenting is not "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some formats define single line comment markers, some multiline markers and "
"some both. If multiline markers are not available, commenting out a "
"selection that does not fully include its last line is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a single line marker is available, commenting single lines is preferred "
"where applicable, as this helps to avoid problems with nested comments."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When removing comment markers, no uncommented text should be selected. When "
"removing multiline comment markers from a selection, any whitespace outside "
"the comment markers is ignored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: advanced.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>comment</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To place comment markers, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Comment</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item or the "
"related keyboard shortcut sequence, default is <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Ctrl;<keycap>D</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: advanced.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>uncomment</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove comment markers, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Uncomment</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item or the "
"related keyboard shortcut, default is <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"&Shift;<keycap>D</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Editor Component Command Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate;'s editor component has an internal command line, allowing you to "
"perform various actions from a minimal GUI. The command line is a text entry "
"in the bottom of the editor area, to show it select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Switch to Command Line</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> or use the shortcut (default is <keycombo action="
"\"simul\"><keycap>F7</keycap></keycombo>). The editor provides a set of "
"commands as documented below, and additional commands can be provided by "
"plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To execute a command, type the command then press the return key. The "
"command line will indicate whether it succeeded and possibly display a "
"message. If you entered the command line by pressing <keycap>F7</keycap> it "
"will automatically hide after a few seconds. To clear the message and enter "
"a new command, press <keycap>F7</keycap> again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The command line has a built-in help system, issue the command "
"<command>help</command> to get started. To see a list of all available "
"commands issue <command>help list</command>, to view help for a specific "
"command, do <command>help <replaceable>command</replaceable></command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The command line has a built in history, so you can reuse commands already "
"typed. To navigate the history, use the <keycap>Up</keycap> and "
"<keycap>Down</keycap> keys. When showing historical commands, the argument "
"part of the command will be selected, allowing you to easily overwrite the "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "Standard Command Line Commands"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands for Configuring the Editor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These commands are provided by the editor component, and allows you to "
"configure the active document and view only. This is handy if you want to "
"use a setting different from the default settings, for example for "
"indentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Argument types"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: advanced.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "BOOLEAN"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is used with commands that turns things on or off. Legal values are "
"<userinput>on</userinput>, <userinput>off</userinput>, <userinput>true</"
"userinput>, <userinput>false</userinput>, <userinput>1</userinput> or "
"<userinput>0</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: advanced.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "INTEGER"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "An integer number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: advanced.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "STRING"
msgstr "CADENA"

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "A string"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-tab-width</command><arg>INTEGER width</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the tab width to the number <userinput>width</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-indent-width</command><arg>INTEGER width</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the indentation width to the number <userinput>width</userinput>. Used "
"only if you are indenting with spaces."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-word-wrap-column</command><arg>INTEGER width</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the line width for hard wrapping to <userinput>width</userinput>. This "
"is used if you are having your text wrapped automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-icon-border</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the visibility of the icon border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-folding-markers</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the visibility of the folding markers pane."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-line-numbers</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets the visibility of the line numbers pane."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-replace-tabs</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "If enabled, tabs are replaced with spaces as you type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-remove-trailing-space</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, trailing whitespace are removed whenever the cursor leaves a "
"line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-show-tabs</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, TAB characters and trailing whitespace will be visualized by a "
"small dot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-indent-spaces</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, the editor will indent with <option>indent-width</option> spaces "
"for each indentation level, rather than with one TAB character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-mixed-indent</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will use a mix of TAB and spaces for indentation. Each "
"indentation level will be <option>indent-width</option> wide, and more "
"indentation levels will be optimized to use as many TAB characters as "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When executed, this command will additionally set space indentation enabled, "
"and if the indent width is unspecified it will be set to half of the "
"<option>tab-width</option> for the document at the time of execution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-word-wrap</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enables dynamic word wrap according to <userinput>enable</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-replace-tabs-save</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable </arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When enabled, tabs will be replaced with whitespace whenever the document is "
"saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>set-remove-trailing-space-save</command><arg>BOOLEAN enable</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When enabled, trailing space will be removed from each line whenever the "
"document is saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-indent-mode</command><arg>name</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the autoindentation mode to <userinput>name</userinput>. If "
"<userinput>name</userinput> is not known, the mode is set to 'none'. Valid "
"modes are 'cstyle', 'csands', 'xml', 'python', 'varindent' and 'none'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>set-highlight</command><arg>highlight</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the syntax highlighting system for the document. The argument must be a "
"valid highlight name, as seen in the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Highlighting</guisubmenu></menuchoice> menu. This "
"command provides an autocompletion list for its argument."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands for editing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "These commands modify the current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: advanced.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "indent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indents the selected lines or the current line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: advanced.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "unindent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Unindents the selected lines or current line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: advanced.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "cleanindent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Cleans up the indentation of the selected lines or current line according to "
"the indentation settings in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: advanced.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>comment</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Inserts comment markers to make the selection or selected lines or current "
"line a comment according to the text format as defined by the syntax "
"highlight definition for the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: advanced.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>uncomment</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Removes comment markers from the selection or selected lines or current line "
"according to the text format as defined by the syntax highlight definition "
"for the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: advanced.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "kill-line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deletes the current line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>replace</command><arg>pattern</arg><arg>replacement</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Replaces text matching <userinput>pattern</userinput> with "
"<userinput>replacement</userinput>. If you want to include whitespace in the "
"<userinput>pattern</userinput>, you must quote both the <userinput>pattern</"
"userinput> and <userinput>replacement</userinput> with single or double "
"quotes. If the arguments are unquoted, the first word is used as "
"<userinput>pattern</userinput> and the rest for <userinput>replacement</"
"userinput>. If <userinput>replacement</userinput> is empty, each occurrence "
"of <userinput>pattern</userinput> is removed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set flags to configure the search by adding a colon, followed by one "
"or more letters each representing a configuration, giving the form "
"<userinput>replace:options pattern replacement</userinput>. Available "
"options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: advanced.docbook:288 advanced.docbook:530 advanced.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>b</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:289 advanced.docbook:531 advanced.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search backwards."
msgstr "Cercar en rèire."

#. Tag: userinput
#: advanced.docbook:293 advanced.docbook:535 advanced.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>c</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:294 advanced.docbook:536 advanced.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search from cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: advanced.docbook:298 advanced.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>e</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:299 advanced.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search in the selection only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: advanced.docbook:303 advanced.docbook:545 advanced.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>r</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:304 advanced.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do regular expression search. If set, you may use <userinput>\\N</userinput> "
"where N is a number to represent captures in the replacement string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: advanced.docbook:310 advanced.docbook:552 advanced.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>s</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:311 advanced.docbook:553 advanced.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do case sensitive search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: advanced.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>p</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prompt for permission to replace the next occurence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: advanced.docbook:320 advanced.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>w</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:321 advanced.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "Match whole words only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: advanced.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>date</command><arg>format</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: advanced.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Inserts a date/time string as defined by the specified <userinput>format</"
"userinput>, or the format <quote>yyyy-MM-dd hh:mm:ss</quote> if none is "
"specified. The following translations are done when interpreting "
"<userinput>format</userinput>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
